Recycling one tonne of aluminium saves 95% of the energy needed to produce it from bauxite ore — aluminium recycling is economically and environmentally compelling regardless of other considerations.
Recycled paper production uses 60% less energy and 50% less water than virgin paper; it also reduces deforestation pressure on biodiverse forest ecosystems.
Producing steel from scrap uses 74% less energy than from iron ore and emits 58% less CO₂ — the steel industry's circular economy model is among the most mature in manufacturing.
